{"event_type":"review","id":"2520436ab6c601e043ca76286dd5fe4012113211088302464cc436b9bedd833f","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T23:15:22Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/31e38497d55db817bd5bacb855be93fdfb693eff7883bae7680bafd861e4388f","sha256":"31e38497d55db817bd5bacb855be93fdfb693eff7883bae7680bafd861e4388f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/58e3853d3e7750324aff6bc4226c3dbc3aa95cf41abb700b9ecff5ae43590f22","sha256":"58e3853d3e7750324aff6bc4226c3dbc3aa95cf41abb700b9ecff5ae43590f22"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8f4e6f68b66d3ea68a98077987ec866f0375b90a9b2574f35511bebb469895ae","sha256":"8f4e6f68b66d3ea68a98077987ec866f0375b90a9b2574f35511bebb469895ae"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/55583348541e53e6e0fa18f2c8dad6a5bb301308c683d581bc7750ba224c33d6","sha256":"55583348541e53e6e0fa18f2c8dad6a5bb301308c683d581bc7750ba224c33d6"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/45b6ff71cf3cbd714eb345e6890481b9ec9579b7c57391baf5c11c3abee80e1d","sha256":"45b6ff71cf3cbd714eb345e6890481b9ec9579b7c57391baf5c11c3abee80e1d"}],"attempt_id":"2066cde87636fc82c501846eabe10aae90cf0556f8d8c3fa3ac5b33db1d9bbd9:0:1","base":"d8f0efbba47c37498b5e65597092d40aa3123957","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"02f29f086668d7fed05544909d70500507191efd","body":"**Measure the same runtime directory that `ExecStart` executes.**\n\nWhen `options.artifactRoot` is supplied, `renderService` measures that override path. The rendered `ExecStart` still uses the `home`-derived install path. The returned `artifact` can therefore describe a different directory from the one the unit runs. A consumer that treats `artifact` as evidence for `execStart` can accept identity for the wrong install. Either derive the measured path from `home` when the identity must match `ExecStart`, or reject an `artifactRoot` that differs from that path. If the override is intended for staging, document that `artifact` describes the staged root and not the executed runtime.","id":"ac91b136aba1c9d815c30a3351a911cfc0f1ed520fad165f2ab0c48017fe6d92","intervals":[[126,126]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/renderService.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Measure the same runtime directory that `ExecStart` executes."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"81c23f5d1a0cd6c6580d88dd5139f552a7ac40c4","body":"**Reject journaled snapshots whose runtime differs from `prior_runtime`.**\n\n`switchUnit` accepts any snapshot that `adapter.validateSnapshot` allows, then journals it unchanged. `recoverUnit` later refuses a record whose `snapshot.runtime` does not equal `prior_runtime`. A snapshot that the adapter accepts without a matching `runtime` therefore produces a pending journal record that recovery cannot read.\n\nAdd the same check before the journal is written:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     const snapshot = await adapter.snapshot(unit);\n     await adapter.validateSnapshot(unit, snapshot);\n+    if (!isDict(snapshot) || get(snapshot, 'runtime') !== prior['runtime']) {\n+      throw new RecordRefused('snapshot runtime does not match prior runtime');\n+    }\n     let identity: Dict = {\n```\n\n</details>","id":"d14bfb49ae38ab785356b1e71a40213fd5a1dc078eaf18e0041571225f57564d","intervals":[[215,215]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/unitTransaction.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject journaled snapshots whose runtime differs from `priorruntime`."}],"head":"493b8854b375e3b1108cd7ecf79fd21996e2d4f0","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"ec94ba835aaa56095bdaed06449e54f0f3efd48e","intervals":[[1,293]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/controllerHealth.ts"},{"blob":"44